1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,702
July second, nineteen thirty seven.

2
00:00:02,922 --> 00:00:08,907
A Coast Guard ship sits next to a tiny Pacific island, pumping black smoke into the sky.

3
00:00:09,407 --> 00:00:13,135
It's a signal for Amelia Earhart, who is supposed to land there.

4
00:00:14,535 --> 00:00:16,687
Then her voice comes over the radio.

5
00:00:16,907 --> 00:00:18,892
We must be on you, but cannot see you.

6
00:00:19,112 --> 00:00:20,447
Gas is running low.

7
00:00:20,947 --> 00:00:22,145
The crew could hear her.

8
00:00:22,365 --> 00:00:23,442
She couldn't hear them.

9
00:00:23,662 --> 00:00:26,036
An hour later, the radio went silent.

10
00:00:26,256 --> 00:00:27,549
She was never found.

11
00:00:28,949 --> 00:00:31,198
The island was just over a mile long.

12
00:00:31,418 --> 00:00:33,688
Somewhere close, she flew right past it.

13
00:00:34,188 --> 00:00:36,916
Follow for true stories history never finished.
